+
+## Recovery
+
+`harnie backup <path>` writes a consistent snapshot of the live SQLite
+store. The output file is created with owner-only permissions (`0600`) so
+it matches the store's own protection.
+
+```sh
+harnie backup /path/to/harnie.db.bak
+```
+
+`harnie restore <path> --force` validates the backup file first, then
+overwrites the live store with the snapshot. Restore is destructive: it
+has no undo, so make sure the backup is the state you want before passing
+`--force`.
+
+```sh
+harnie restore /path/to/harnie.db.bak --force
+```
